  "definition": "Tight mark: nearest outfield opponent within 3.0 m at frame_start. Goalkeepers are excluded. Drawn out: mean Euclidean distance, in metres, of the centre-backs, central midfielders, or full backs from that role acronym's median position for the same defending team and the same block in the match. The median uses a 2 Hz sample of organized-block frames in attack-normalized coordinates and needs at least 8 samples. Role acronyms come from the match json, with the modal event position used only when the squad role is missing or SUB. The interval resamples matches. A role is supported only when that interval lies entirely above zero. For lead_to_shot, xthreat, and line_break, supported means the interval excludes zero in either direction. xthreat is player_targeted_xthreat on the possession. line_break is first_line_break. Hungarian sensitivity: goal-side assignment from coupled_formation.hungarian_marking within 3.0 m. It does not decide drawn_out_roles.",
